msgid "**Advanced Security:** Incorporates TLS encryption, DKIM, and SPF to secure your communications and prevent spoofing."
msgstr "**Sécurité avancée :** Incorpore le cryptage TLS, DKIM et SPF pour sécuriser vos communications et empêcher le spoofing."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced openresty load-balancing strategies.** v1 uses default round-robin in the per-app `upstream` block. Weighted distribution, least-connections, sticky sessions (`ip_hash` / cookie-based), and active HTTP healthchecks are out of scope. Adding them is a follow-up requirement and only becomes load-bearing once a service is regularly run with replicas > 1, which itself depends on shared storage being NFS-backed for that service."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent VM template:** ``files/vm-template/`` holds the package list and the ``rootfs/`` tree of the agent VM image that ``make agents-vm-template`` builds. The build checks the sha256 of every runtime tarball and of ``act`` it downloads, refuses a sum that is not 64 lowercase hex digits, and installs the runtimes with ``npm install --ignore-scripts``. Known gap, dependencies unverified: npm resolves the dependencies of each runtime tarball from the registry without a lockfile or a checked sum."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent VM template:** `files/vm-template/` holds the package list and the `rootfs/` tree of the agent VM image that `make agents-vm-template` builds. The build checks the sha256 of every runtime tarball and of `act` it downloads, refuses a sum that is not 64 lowercase hex digits, and installs the runtimes with `npm install --ignore-scripts`. Known gap, dependencies unverified: npm resolves the dependencies of each runtime tarball from the registry without a lockfile or a checked sum."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent bridge:** ``services.incus.network`` is a bridge without NAT and without IPv6, so a VM leaves the host only through the egress proxy the agent firewall compiles."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent bridge:** `services.incus.network` is a bridge without NAT and without IPv6, so a VM leaves the host only through the egress proxy the agent firewall compiles."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent dashboards are public behind proxy + Keycloak OIDC.** `web-app-hermes` and `web-app-openclaw` follow the standard `web-app-*` contract: own canonical domain, reverse-proxy routing, SSO enforced via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/). Hermes uses its native self-hosted OIDC support. OpenClaw's native OIDC is unverified upstream: if absent, the dashboard sits behind the platform's standard auth-proxy pattern (SSO enforced at the proxy, OpenClaw's own token auth staying internal-only). No unauthenticated public surface either way."
msgstr "**Les tableaux de bord des agents sont publics derrière le proxy + Keycloak OIDC.** `web-app-hermes` et `web-app-openclaw` suivre la norme `web-app-*` contrat: domaine canonique propre, routage inverse-proxy, SSO [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/). Hermes utilise son support OIDC natif auto-organisé. OIDC natif d'OpenClaw est non vérifié en amont : en cas d'absence, le tableau de bord se trouve derrière le modèle standard d'auth-proxy de la plateforme (SSO appliqué au proxy, jeton propre d'OpenClaw auth rester interne-seulement)Pas de surface publique non authentifiée."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent gateway:** The container runs the OpenClaw gateway bound to the LAN interface on port 18789, with an HTTP health check against `/healthz`."
msgstr "**Porte de l'agent :** Le conteneur exécute la passerelle OpenClaw liée à l'interface LAN sur le port 18789, avec un contrôle de santé HTTP contre `/healthz`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent gateway:** The container runs the OpenClaw gateway bound to the LAN interface on port 18789, with an HTTP health check against ``/healthz``."
msgstr "**Porte de l'agent :** Le conteneur exécute la passerelle OpenClaw liée à l'interface LAN sur le port 18789, avec un contrôle de santé HTTP contre ``/healthz``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent receiver:** Container port 8000 is mapped to a host port (``local.agent``); external proxying for remote-host TLS agent registration is a follow-up."
msgstr "**Récepteur d'agent:** Port de conteneurs 8000 est cartographié vers un port hôte (``local.agent``); mandataire externe pour l'enregistrement d'un agent TLS à distance est un suivi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent receiver:** Container port 8000 is mapped to a host port (`local.agent`); external proxying for remote-host TLS agent registration is a follow-up."
msgstr "**Récepteur d'agent:** Port de conteneurs 8000 est cartographié vers un port hôte (`local.agent`); mandataire externe pour l'enregistrement d'un agent TLS à distance est un suivi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent reuse:** The embodied deployment is the agent role itself, so image, configuration and model routing stay identical to the isolated deployments."
msgstr "**Réutilisation des agents :** Le déploiement incarné est le rôle d'agent lui-même, de sorte que l'image, la configuration et le routage du modèle restent identiques aux déploiements isolés."

msgid "**Agent sandbox.** *git commit --amend* is denied, the host's credential files stay unreadable inside the sandbox, sandboxed commands may reach local services on 127.0.0.1 to 127.0.0.12 and localhost, and third-party plugins are no longer switched on for every contributor."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent-aware:** an agent role on the same host brings its editor extension along."
msgstr "**Agent averti :** un rôle d'agent sur le même hôte apporte son extension d'éditeur."

msgid "**Agent-driven modelling:** An MCP client creates, edits and renders scenes through Blender's own Python API."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent-driven modelling:** An MCP client creates, edits and renders scenes through Blender’s own Python API."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents as employees, with a kernel between them and the host.** *web-app-hermes* and *web-app-openclaw* deploy agents behind the single sign-on gate, wired to the gateway's models and to the MCP servers discovery hands them, each proving on deploy that it can actually reach them. *svc-virt-kata* runs that tier under a kernel-isolating container runtime, and *svc-ai-robot* embodies an agent on a dedicated device. Every sandboxed agent acts as its own platform account rather than borrowing yours. See [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) and [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."
msgstr "**Agents en tant qu'employés, avec un noyau entre eux et l'hôte.** *web-app-hermes* et *web-app-openclaw* déployer des agents derrière la porte d'accès unique, branchés aux modèles de la passerelle et à la découverte des serveurs MCP, chacun prouvant sur déploiement qu'il peut effectivement les atteindre. *svc-virt-kata* exécute ce niveau dans un conteneur isolant, et *svc-ai-robot* incarne un agent sur un appareil dédié. Chaque agent sandboxé agit comme son propre compte de plateforme plutôt que d'emprunter le vôtre. Voir [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) et [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."

msgid "**Agents consume tools as MCP clients via the [050](050-mcp-role-integration.md) mechanism.** Hermes and OpenClaw are configured as MCP clients of the repository's MCP server roles over HTTP/SSE (not stdio: under microVM isolation and multi-node placement a stdio subprocess cannot reach an MCP server in another container). Discovery and credentials reuse 050's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) lookup and `credentials:` blocks. Both roles are added to 050's MCP audit as client roles. Only 050's shared contract (the `services.mcp` schema) and the lookup extension are prerequisites for this requirement; 050's audit tooling, full lint set, and baserow+openwebui slice are independent later work."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for ``hermes`` or ``openclaw`` creates that user’s agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr "**Agents sur demande:** La première réalisation d'un utilisateur pour ``hermes`` ou ``openclaw`` crée cet agent utilisateur; demande plus tard de le réutiliser, et un agent arrêté est recommencé avec son volume d'état ré-attaché."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for `hermes` or `openclaw` creates that user's agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr "**Agents sur demande:** La première réalisation d'un utilisateur pour `hermes` ou `openclaw` crée l'agent de cet utilisateur; demande plus tard de le réutiliser, et un agent arrêté est recommencé avec son volume d'état ré-attaché."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents that spin up containers use nested Docker inside the isolated runtime; host socket passthrough is forbidden.** When an agent needs to run compose workloads (see the scenario below), it runs a nested Docker daemon inside its own isolated runtime. Mounting the host `/var/run/docker.sock` into an agent that executes model-generated code is **forbidden**: it grants root-equivalent host control and defeats the isolation entirely. Nested Docker costs performance and, on gVisor, may need `runsc` with the appropriate platform; the role README MUST document the overhead. An agent role that requires containers MUST declare this capability explicitly."
msgstr "**Les agents qui font tourner les conteneurs utilisent Docker imbriqué à l'intérieur de l'exécution isolée; la transmission de la prise hôte est interdite.** Quand un agent doit exécuter composer des charges de travail (voir le scénario ci-dessous), il dirige un démon Docker imbriqué dans son propre runtime isolé. Monter l'hôte `/var/run/docker.sock` dans un agent qui exécute le code généré par le modèle est **interdit**: il accorde un contrôle d'hôte équivalent à la racine et défait entièrement l'isolement. La performance des coûts de Docker imbriqué et, sur gVisor, peut avoir besoin `runsc` avec la plateforme appropriée; le rôle README DOIT documenter les frais généraux. Un rôle d'agent qui nécessite des conteneurs DOIT déclarer cette capacité explicitement."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agile Boards & Scrum/Kanban Integration:** Manage agile projects using Scrum or Kanban boards, track progress through sprints, and maintain a clear overview of work in progress."
msgstr "**Conseils agiles & Intégration Scrum/Kanban :** Gérer les projets agiles à l'aide de planches Scrum ou Kanban, suivre les progrès au moyen de sprints et maintenir un aperçu clair des travaux en cours."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules live in the role that owns the metric.** A role ships its Prometheus rules in *templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2*. The new *alert_rule_roles* lookup includes them only for roles that Prometheus actually scrapes, so a rules file needs no activation check of its own. It must start at the *groups:* item level. OpenBao's seal alert is the first rule to use it."
msgstr "**Les règles d'alerte vivent dans le rôle qui appartient à la métrique.** Un rôle expédie ses règles Prométhée dans *templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2*. La nouvelle *alert_rule_roles* recherche les inclut seulement pour les rôles que Prometheus en fait gratte, donc un fichier de règles n'a pas besoin de vérification d'activation de son propre. Il doit commencer par *Groupes:* Niveau. Ouvrir L'alerte de Bao est la première règle pour l'utiliser."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules ship with the role.** ``templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2`` is discovered by the ``alert_rule_roles`` lookup, which returns only roles that are actually scraped, so the fragment carries no activation guard of its own. It must start at the ``groups:`` item level."
msgstr "**Alert règle le vaisseau avec le rôle.** ``templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2`` est découvert par le ``alert_rule_roles`` recherche, qui ne retourne que des rôles qui sont effectivement grattés, de sorte que le fragment ne porte pas de garde d'activation propre. Il doit commencer par ``groups:`` Niveau."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules ship with the role.** `templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2` is discovered by the `alert_rule_roles` lookup, which returns only roles that are actually scraped, so the fragment carries no activation guard of its own. It must start at the `groups:` item level."
msgstr "**Alert règle le vaisseau avec le rôle.** `templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2` est découvert par le `alert_rule_roles` recherche, qui ne retourne que des rôles qui sont effectivement grattés, de sorte que le fragment ne porte pas de garde d'activation propre. Il doit commencer par `groups:` Niveau."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alerting Support:** Works with the [`sys-ctl-alm-compose`](../sys-ctl-alm-compose/README.md) role for failure notifications."
msgstr "**Soutien à l'alerte :** Fonctionne avec le [`sys-ctl-alm-compose`](../sys-ctl-alm-compose/README.md) rôle des notifications de défaillance."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alerting Support:** Works with the ```sys-ctl-alm-compose`` <../sys-ctl-alm-compose/README.md>`__ role for failure notifications."
msgstr "**Soutien à l'alerte :** Fonctionne avec le ```sys-ctl-alm-compose`` <../sys-ctl-alm-compose/README.md>`  rôle pour les notifications d'échec."

msgid "**Alerting** (``templates/provisioning/alerting.yml.j2``): the rule ``GRAFANA_LOG_ALERT_TITLE`` (``Critical line in an application log``) fires on ``services.loki.alerting.critical_pattern`` of ``web-svc-loki`` in the ``application`` log class and notifies the Alertmanager of ``web-app-prometheus`` through the contact point ``GRAFANA_ALERTMANAGER_RECEIVER``; the Alertmanager’s receivers (email, Telegram, Mattermost) are the existing alert channels. The Loki ruler raises the same alert independently. The reverse proxy’s access log is the ``access`` log class (see `log collector <../sys-svc-log-collector/README.md>`__), so an access log line raises neither; a line of the proxy’s error log that carries the request path still raises both. ``files/playwright/test-alerting.js`` uses that error log path to write a line with the word ``critical``: it requests a file the CDN location ``CDN_RELATIVE_ROOT`` does not hold, which the proxy answers with 404 and logs with its path. It then waits until the rule fires for that application, and, with Prometheus deployed, until the contact point delivered the alert to the Alertmanager without error."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Alerting** (`templates/provisioning/alerting.yml.j2`): the rule `GRAFANA_LOG_ALERT_TITLE` (`Critical line in an application log`) fires on `services.loki.alerting.critical_pattern` of `web-svc-loki` in the `application` log class and notifies the Alertmanager of `web-app-prometheus` through the contact point `GRAFANA_ALERTMANAGER_RECEIVER`; the Alertmanager's receivers (email, Telegram, Mattermost) are the existing alert channels. The Loki ruler raises the same alert independently. The reverse proxy's access log is the `access` log class (see [log collector](../sys-svc-log-collector/README.md)), so an access log line raises neither; a line of the proxy's error log that carries the request path still raises both. `files/playwright/test-alerting.js` uses that error log path to write a line with the word `critical`: it requests a file the CDN location `CDN_RELATIVE_ROOT` does not hold, which the proxy answers with 404 and logs with its path. It then waits until the rule fires for that application, and, with Prometheus deployed, until the contact point delivered the alert to the Alertmanager without error."
msgstr ""

