msgid "**Directory Profile:** ``user_ldap`` syncs phone, website, organisation, title, description, quota and avatar from the directory, and Nextcloud shows those profile fields read-only. `files/python/ldap_refresh.py <./files/python/ldap_refresh.py>`__ runs ``occ ldap:check-user --update`` for every directory account Nextcloud already knows, as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer, so a profile changed in Keycloak arrives without a native LDAP login. The same hook composes street, postal code, city, region and country of the directory entry into the address and sets it with ``occ user:profile``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory Profile:** `user_ldap` syncs phone, website, organisation, title, description, quota and avatar from the directory, and Nextcloud shows those profile fields read-only. [files/python/ldap_refresh.py](./files/python/ldap_refresh.py) runs `occ ldap:check-user --update` for every directory account Nextcloud already knows, as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer, so a profile changed in Keycloak arrives without a native LDAP login. The same hook composes street, postal code, city, region and country of the directory entry into the address and sets it with `occ user:profile`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory delegations off against old ganesha:** When the server runs nfs-ganesha older than 9.11, every client and the controller set the kernel's `nfsv4` parameter `directory_delegations` to `N`, at runtime and in `/etc/modprobe.d`. The parameter is kernel-wide, so on a lab whose nodes share one kernel it covers every NFS mount of that host until the module reloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory delegations off against old ganesha:** When the server runs nfs-ganesha older than 9.11, every client and the controller set the kernel’s ``nfsv4`` parameter ``directory_delegations`` to ``N``, at runtime and in ``/etc/modprobe.d``. The parameter is kernel-wide, so on a lab whose nodes share one kernel it covers every NFS mount of that host until the module reloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Directory full names:** the same hook sets the full name of every Penpot profile whose e-mail the directory holds to the directory's name, because Penpot takes the name from OIDC or LDAP only when it registers the profile."
