# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at `/openbao/policies/`, because OpenBao parses *every* file under `-config` as server configuration. Storage is `/openbao/file`, not `/openbao/data`: the image pre-chowns only `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` for the non-root `openbao` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. `command:` is just `server` — the entrypoint appends `-config` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Les chemins qui ont l'air mauvais et ne le sont pas.** Les politiques montent à `/openbao/policies/`, parce que OpenBao analyse *chaque* fichier sous `-config` comme configuration du serveur. Le stockage est `/openbao/file`, Pas `/openbao/data`: l'image pré-chowns seulement `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` pour les non-racines `openbao` l'utilisateur, donc un volume ailleurs débarque la propriété racine et le radeau ne peut pas écrire. `command:` est juste `server` — les appendices du point d'entrée `-config` lui-même, et le passer duplicate le drapeau."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at ``/openbao/policies/``, because OpenBao parses *every* file under ``-config`` as server configuration. Storage is ``/openbao/file``, not ``/openbao/data``: the image pre-chowns only ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` for the non-root ``openbao`` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. ``command:`` is just ``server`` — the entrypoint appends ``-config`` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Les chemins qui ont l'air mauvais et ne le sont pas.** Les politiques montent à ``/openbao/policies/``, parce que OpenBao analyse *chaque* fichier sous ``-config`` comme configuration du serveur. Le stockage est ``/openbao/file``, Pas ``/openbao/data``: l'image pré-chowns seulement ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` pour les non-racines ``openbao`` l'utilisateur, donc un volume ailleurs débarque la propriété racine et le radeau ne peut pas écrire. ``command:`` est juste ``server`` — les appendices du point d'entrée ``-config`` lui-même, et le passer duplicate le drapeau."

msgid "**Pause and resume:** ``app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all`` runs ``compose down`` and ``compose up -d`` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application’s own ``*.infinito.nexus`` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Pause and resume:** `app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all` runs `compose down` and `compose up -d` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application's own `*.infinito.nexus` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page.** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a page that shows an animation of a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, states that the service is paused, and lists the platform operator's contact channels from `service_provider.contact` (email, Mastodon and the others declared there). The page text is multilingual and managed through the `core` `.po` catalogs."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of ``service_provider.contact``. The page is rendered from the ``core`` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from ``Accept-Language``, with English as the fallback."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of `service_provider.contact`. The page is rendered from the `core` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from `Accept-Language`, with English as the fallback."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice, and every contact channel of ``service_provider.contact``. One page is rendered per language the ``core`` catalogs translate; nginx picks it from ``Accept-Language`` and falls back to English."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice, and every contact channel of `service_provider.contact`. One page is rendered per language the `core` catalogs translate; nginx picks it from `Accept-Language` and falls back to English."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused state.** Pausing leaves no running instance of the application: in compose its containers and `*.infinito.nexus` timers stop, in swarm every service of its stack runs 0 replicas. Resuming restores the declared state."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-Consumer Isolation:** Each consumer gets a role and user scoped to its own `<entity>-*` index namespace."
msgstr "**Isolation par consommateur :** Chaque consommateur a un rôle à jouer et l'utilisateur a une portée propre `<entity>-*` espace de noms d'index."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-Consumer Isolation:** Each consumer gets a role and user scoped to its own ``<entity>-*`` index namespace."
msgstr "**Isolation par consommateur :** Chaque consommateur a un rôle à jouer et l'utilisateur a une portée propre ``<entity>-*`` espace de noms d'index."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-Consumer Isolation:** Issues a scoped API key per consumer, restricted to its own collection namespace."
msgstr "**Isolation par consommateur :** Émet une clé API étendue par consommateur, limitée à son propre espace de noms de collection."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Per-Consumer Isolation:** OSS Qdrant has no per-user auth; each consumer is isolated by the collection-name prefix ``{entity}_``."
msgstr "**Isolation par consommateur :** OSS Qdrant n'a pas d'auth par utilisateur; chaque consommateur est isolé par le préfixe du nom de collection ``{entity}_``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Per-Consumer Isolation:** OSS Qdrant has no per-user auth; each consumer is isolated by the collection-name prefix `{entity}_`."
msgstr "**Isolation par consommateur :** OSS Qdrant n'a pas d'auth par utilisateur; chaque consommateur est isolé par le préfixe du nom de collection `{entity}_`."

msgid "**Per-app RBAC:** Members of `/roles/web-app-kix/administrator` or `/roles/web-app-kix/user` are admitted to KIX; other users are blocked at the OAuth2 proxy. On every sign-in `GroupDNBasedRoleSync` sets the KIX roles from the role groups: `administrator` grants `Superuser`, `user` grants `Ticket Agent`, and a role the user no longer holds is revoked."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Per-app RBAC:** Members of ``/roles/web-app-kix/administrator`` or ``/roles/web-app-kix/user`` are admitted to KIX; other users are blocked at the OAuth2 proxy. On every sign-in ``GroupDNBasedRoleSync`` sets the KIX roles from the role groups: ``administrator`` grants ``Superuser``, ``user`` grants ``Ticket Agent``, and a role the user no longer holds is revoked."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Per-application timeout:** Every collector is cut off after `SYS_TIMEOUT_CLEANUP_APP`, on the host and inside the container, where a killed `docker exec` client would leave the work running."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Per-application timeout:** Every collector is cut off after ``SYS_TIMEOUT_CLEANUP_APP``, on the host and inside the container, where a killed ``docker exec`` client would leave the work running."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-consumer isolation:** Every consumer receives its own identity and bucket with bucket-scoped actions only."
msgstr "**Isolement des consommateurs:** Chaque consommateur reçoit sa propre identité et son propre seau avec des actions seau-scoped seulement."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-consumer virtual keys:** Each consuming application receives its own virtual key, created through the gateway admin API under an alias naming that application."
msgstr "**Clés virtuelles par consommateur :** Chaque application consommatrice reçoit sa propre clé virtuelle, créée par l'API d'administration de passerelle sous un pseudonyme de cette application."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-container snapshots:** rsync `--link-dest` snapshots deduplicate unchanged files across runs."
msgstr "**Photographies par conteneur :** Rsync `--link-dest` snapshots dédoublent les fichiers inchangés à travers les runs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-container snapshots:** rsync ``--link-dest`` snapshots deduplicate unchanged files across runs."
msgstr "**Photographies par conteneur :** Rsync ``--link-dest`` snapshots dédoublent les fichiers inchangés à travers les runs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-domain TLS via app-level override**: extra public domains under `applications.<app>.server.domains` deploy as additional HTTPS vhosts; flavor from `applications.<app>.tls.mode` (default `TLS_MODE`). `.onion` → always HTTP. No per-domain TLS map."
msgstr "**TLS par domaine via l'application-niveau de redéfinition**: domaines extra publics `applications.<app>.server.domains` déployer comme vhosts HTTPS supplémentaires; saveur de `applications.<app>.tls.mode` (par défaut `TLS_MODE`). `.onion` → toujours HTTP. Aucune carte TLS par domaine."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-family dispatch:** Routes by ``ansible_facts['distribution']`` so the caller never has to gate the role with a ``when:`` clause."
msgstr "**Expédition par famille:** Itinéraires par ``ansible_facts['distribution']`` donc l'appelant n'a jamais à entrer le rôle avec un ``when:`` clause."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-family dispatch:** Routes by `ansible_facts['distribution']` so the caller never has to gate the role with a `when:` clause."
msgstr "**Expédition par famille:** Itinéraires par `ansible_facts['distribution']` donc l'appelant n'a jamais à entrer le rôle avec un `when:` clause."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-role opt-IN** on a non-swarm host: explicitly rejected. Swarm mode is exclusively triggered by group membership. The per-role `DEPLOYMENT_MODE` override only opts OUT on a swarm host, never opts IN on a non-swarm host."
msgstr "**Opt-IN par rôle** sur un hôte non chaud: explicitement rejeté. Le mode Swarm est exclusivement déclenché par l'adhésion au groupe. Le rôle `DEPLOYMENT_MODE` ne remplace que OUT sur un hôte d'essaim, ne choisit jamais IN sur un hôte non chaud."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-role opt-OUT** on a swarm host: a role MAY override `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: compose` in its `vars/main.yml` to stay on the compose path even when the host is in `svc-swarm-node`. Role vars win over `group_vars/all` by Ansible precedence."
msgstr "**Choix par rôle** sur un hôte d'essaim: un rôle PEUT dépasser `DEPLOYMENT_MODE: compose` dans ses `vars/main.yml` pour rester sur le chemin de composition même lorsque l'hôte est en `svc-swarm-node`. Le rôle gagne `group_vars/all` par Préséance Ansible."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Per-round variant selection.** In round R every primary app uses variant index `R if R < its_variant_count else 0`. So a single-variant app stays on variant 0 in every round, and a 3-variant app in a 5-round deploy follows `0, 1, 2, 0, 0`."
msgstr "**Sélection des variantes par tour.** En ronde R chaque application primaire utilise un indice de variante `R if R < its_variant_count else 0`. Donc une application monovariante reste sur la variante 0 dans chaque tour, et un 3-variante application dans une 5-déploiement rond suivant `0, 1, 2, 0, 0`."

msgid "**Per-vhost decisions.** One vhost per sibling. TLS, injected snippets, CSP, redirects and health probes are decided by the vhost domain, and every cross-app URL rendered into a vhost comes from that vhost's network."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Per-vhost parameters move into meta, per domain, without exceptions.** Every value an include site passes today moves into the role's meta, keyed by domain. This includes the multi-vhost roles (Matrix, Stalwart, Bluesky and the others listed below)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Per-vhost parameters passed at call sites:** `domain`, `http_port`, `proxy_internal_port`, `webserver_proxy_service_key`, `webserver_vhost_flavour`, `webserver_websocket_location`, `webserver_client_max_body_size`, `webserver_extra_configuration`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Performance Enhancement:** Ensures adequate swap space for optimal system performance."
msgstr "**Amélioration du rendement :** Assure un espace d'échange adéquat pour une performance optimale du système."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Performance Optimization:** Improves overall system performance by leveraging appropriate storage media."
msgstr "**Optimisation des performances :** Améliore la performance globale du système en tirant parti des supports de stockage appropriés."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Performance trade‑off:** While slightly more storage might be used compared to `latin1`, the universality of `utf8mb4` outweighs the cost for most deployments."
msgstr "**Échange de résultats:** Bien qu'un peu plus de stockage puisse être utilisé par rapport à `latin1`, l ' universalité `utf8mb4` dépasse le coût de la plupart des déploiements."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Permissions:** Ensure you have the necessary permissions and rights within the Docker container to perform these actions."
msgstr "**Autorisations:** Assurez-vous d'avoir les autorisations et les droits nécessaires dans le conteneur Docker pour effectuer ces actions."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Persisted on the deploy target** for `INFINITO_VERSION`, written by the [sys-version](../../../roles/sys-version/) role."
msgstr "**Persisté sur la cible de déploiement** pour `INFINITO_VERSION`, écrit par le [sys-version](../../../roles/sys-version/) rôle."

msgid "**Persisted state marker:** `<instance>/.app-control-state` holds `started` or `stopped` and is the single source of truth. Without a marker, the application is created in the `status` of its `services.semaphore` entry; a redeploy brings the application up, configures it, and pauses it again when its marker says `stopped`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Persisted state marker:** ``<instance>/.app-control-state`` holds ``started`` or ``stopped`` and is the single source of truth. Without a marker, the application is created in the ``status`` of its ``services.semaphore`` entry; a redeploy brings the application up, configures it, and pauses it again when its marker says ``stopped``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Persistent Timers:** Optionally enables persistent timer behavior to ensure missed activations are handled."
msgstr "**Minuteurs persistants:** En option, permet un comportement de minuteur persistant pour s'assurer que les activations manquées sont gérées."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Persistent agent data:** Agent state is stored in a named volume mounted at `/opt/data`, which the Backup Docker Volumes service captures without stopping the container."
msgstr "**Données sur les agents persistants:** État agent est stocké dans un volume nommé monté à `/opt/data`, que le service Backup Docker Volumes capture sans arrêter le conteneur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
