msgstr "**Inverser-Proxy Ready:** Ensembles ``ATL_PROXY_NAME/PORT/SCHEME/SECURE`` donc Confluence génère des URLs externes correctes derrière HTTPS."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-Proxy/HTTPS Ready:** Preconfigured Atlassian Tomcat proxy envs so Jira respects external scheme/host/port."
msgstr "**Proxy inverse/HTTPS Prêt :** Préconfiguré Atlassian Tomcat proxy envs donc Jira respecte externe scheme/host/port."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** Renders a ``configuration.yaml`` with ``default_config``, ``use_x_forwarded_for``, and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs listed in ``trusted_proxies``. In swarm the hub joins the proxy’s own overlay, so the forwarded request arrives from that network rather than from the hub’s, and trusting only the hub’s subnet makes Home Assistant answer every proxied request with HTTP 400."
msgstr "**Confiance à l'inverse :** Rendre a ``configuration.yaml`` avec ``default_config``, ``use_x_forwarded_for``, ainsi que les DICI de confiance à l'échelle du projet ``trusted_proxies``. Dans l'essaim le hub rejoint le proxys propre superposition, de sorte que la requête transmise arrive de ce réseau plutôt que du hubs, et en faisant confiance seulement le sous-net hubs rend Home Assistant répondre à chaque requête proxiée avec HTTP 400."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** Renders a `configuration.yaml` with `default_config`, `use_x_forwarded_for`, and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs listed in `trusted_proxies`. In swarm the hub joins the proxy's own overlay, so the forwarded request arrives from that network rather than from the hub's, and trusting only the hub's subnet makes Home Assistant answer every proxied request with HTTP 400."
msgstr "**Confiance à l'inverse :** Rendre a `configuration.yaml` avec `default_config`, `use_x_forwarded_for`, ainsi que les DICI de confiance à l'échelle du projet `trusted_proxies`. Dans l'essaim le hub rejoint le propre relais du proxy, de sorte que la requête transmise arrive de ce réseau plutôt que de celui du hub, et en se fiant seulement au sous-net du hub fait Home Assistant répondre chaque requête proxiée avec HTTP 400."

msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** ``gateway.trustedProxies`` carries only the address space the front proxy connects from: the role subnet pool (``NETWORK_ROLE_SUBNET_POOL``) in compose mode, where the proxy reaches the published port through a role network gateway, and Docker’s default overlay pool in swarm mode. Loopback and the other private ranges are no longer trusted. Without the proxy’s source the gateway answers a Control UI WebSocket that arrives with forwarded headers with ``trusted_proxy_untrusted_source`` and closes it before the pairing step, which the Control UI reports as a network failure rather than as a pairing prompt."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** `gateway.trustedProxies` carries only the address space the front proxy connects from: the role subnet pool (`NETWORK_ROLE_SUBNET_POOL`) in compose mode, where the proxy reaches the published port through a role network gateway, and Docker's default overlay pool in swarm mode. Loopback and the other private ranges are no longer trusted. Without the proxy's source the gateway answers a Control UI WebSocket that arrives with forwarded headers with `trusted_proxy_untrusted_source` and closes it before the pairing step, which the Control UI reports as a network failure rather than as a pairing prompt."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review gallery.** Each role gets its own private Artifact with at least 20 views, each captured in light and dark mode and in a desktop (1440×900) and a mobile (390×844) viewport, so at least 80 screenshots of the designed state per role. The views favour detail-rich surfaces: settings, administration, forms, lists and detail pages, logged in where the app has accounts, with idempotently seeded showcase content where a list or detail page would otherwise be empty. `make design-gallery app=<role>` captures them in one spec run and copies them to `/tmp/design-gallery/<role>/`. A comparison with the app before the design is captured on request only: `before=true` adds every view with every injected snippet stripped from the document (the body filter wraps its injections in `<!--infinito-inj-->` markers). The operator approves or rejects by comment."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review workflow:** a translation becomes authoritative when a reviewer approves it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review:** the review page shows the requester, the application, each requested role with its group path, the reason, and the requester's live groups. The approver can deselect roles before confirming."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review:** the review page shows the requester, the application, each requested role with its group path, the reason, and the requester’s live groups. The approver can deselect roles before confirming."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reviewed strings win:** a string approved in [`web-app-weblate`](../web-app-weblate/) is returned verbatim and no engine is called."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reviewed strings win:** a string approved in ```web-app-weblate`` <../web-app-weblate/>`__ is returned verbatim and no engine is called."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Revoke a host:** clear its ``gateway_host``, re-run the pass and deploy the gateway host. The pass drops the host’s URL, model and key, and the gateway deletes every ``host:`` key no consuming host holds any more."
msgstr ""

