# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An address is matched before that, on the raw text, because a URL carries the characters the stripping removes."
msgstr "Une adresse est assortie avant cela, sur le texte brut, parce qu'une URL porte les caractères que le stripping supprime."

msgid "An agent is a role. A role has one soul with one `## Objective`, runs one or more skills, and each skill builds on zero or more routines. Work flows top down: a role runs skills, a skill builds on routines, a routine calls `cli/` and `utils/`. A routine never calls a skill, a skill never calls a role."
msgstr ""

msgid "An agent's `account` grants form an ordered list: the order of its `firewall_roles` binding, then the rule order inside each role, with inventory overrides able to reorder it."
msgstr ""

msgid "An agent's account grants form an ordered list. A grant is active only while its credentials are present (in the inventory or provisioned); an inactive grant is skipped. The first active grant is the default account, used by every routine step that needs an account and names none. When a grant goes inactive, the next active one becomes the default."
msgstr ""

msgid "An algorithm change (router parameters such as fall-through order, failure threshold and settle rule; an engine's declared capabilities such as `services.libretranslate-engine.serves`; masking; damage predicate; glossary; client settings) is opened only with a benchmark: a fixed evaluation set per language built from human-reviewed Weblate strings, scored by the chat judge before and after; it must improve at least one language and lower none."
msgstr ""

msgid "An answer about the item is ``OPEN`` or ``CLOSED``, and HTTP 404 or 410 is ``MISSING``. A timeout, a connection error, HTTP 429 and a 5xx answer are retried with a doubling pause before they count. An exhausted rate limit (a 429 that survives the retries, or a 403 that carries ``X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`` or ``Retry-After``) is ``RATE_LIMITED``, with the reset time the tracker announced. Everything else that still fails is ``UNVERIFIED``: a network error, an auth wall, any other status, a body that is not a JSON object and a state the adapter does not know. A tracker that could not be asked therefore never reads as one that said the item is still open."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An app that needs an extra mapper MUST add it through a per-client scope. See [nextcloud.json.j2](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/scopes/nextcloud.json.j2) for the precedent: a dedicated scope holds the Nextcloud-specific UID and quota mappers and is attached only to the Nextcloud client."
msgstr "Une application qui a besoin d'une carte supplémentaire DOIT l'ajouter à travers une portée par client. Voir [nextcloud.json.j2](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/scopes/nextcloud.json.j2) pour le précédent: une portée dédiée contient l'UID spécifique à Nextcloud et les cartes de quota et est jointe uniquement au client Nextcloud."

msgid "An app the background job has not checked yet is not updated until its next run."
msgstr ""

msgid "An app with no resolvable domain yields an empty list, which the caller renders as no ``cookie_domains`` key at all — oauth2-proxy then falls back to a host-only cookie."
msgstr ""

msgid "An append-only hash chain of audit entries."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application SHOULD opt in to `axis: domain` only when its authorisation model is genuinely per-tenant and the tenant axis is the canonical domain. Typical consumer: WordPress Multisite. Applications whose authorisation is one global user set (Nextcloud, Gitea, Keycloak itself) MUST keep `axis: none`."
msgstr "Une demande DOIT opter pour `axis: domain` Ce n'est que lorsque son modèle d'autorisation est véritablement permanent et que l'axe locataire est le domaine canonique. Consommateur typique : WordPress Multisite. Demandes dont l'autorisation est un ensemble d'utilisateurs mondial (Nextcloud, Gitea, Keycloak lui-même) DOIVENT conserver `axis: none`."

msgid "An application gives every member of one of its roles a host below a parent domain by declaring `domains.served` next to `canonical`:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application id is expanded to the service key(s) that role provides; every other token is kept verbatim. Order-preserving, de-duplicated. Used wherever the operator supplies service references (``disable``, include/prune closures) so both spellings resolve identically."
msgstr "Un identifiant d'application est étendu à la clé de service(s) que le rôle fournit; chaque autre jeton est tenu in extenso. Préservation de l'ordre, doublonné. Utilisé partout où l'opérateur fournit des références de service (``disable``, y compris/prune fermetures) Donc les deux orthographes résolvent identiquement."

msgid "An application registers its reconcile as a hook through [tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml](../../tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml). The util writes `hooks/<application_id>/` under `DIR_RBAC_SYNC`, root-only, with `hook.json`, the hook's script and the modules a host hook imports, and runs the hook once with the members the deploy resolved. The timer runs [files/python/script.py](./files/python/script.py) on `SYS_SCHEDULE_MAINTANANCE_RBAC_SYNC`; it reads the members of each hook's role groups anonymously from the directory and runs every hook whose container runs on the node."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application registers its reconcile as a hook through `tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml <../../tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml>`__. The util writes ``hooks/<application_id>/`` under ``DIR_RBAC_SYNC``, root-only, with ``hook.json``, the hook’s script and the modules a host hook imports, and runs the hook once with the members the deploy resolved. The timer runs `files/python/script.py <./files/python/script.py>`__ on ``SYS_SCHEDULE_MAINTANANCE_RBAC_SYNC``; it reads the members of each hook’s role groups anonymously from the directory and runs every hook whose container runs on the node."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application that declares no ``mem_limit`` for that service lets its container inherit the primary entity's, which is sized for the application and not for the engine beside it. The result is then capped at the same share of the provider's own limit. An application that declares the limit itself is not capped."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application that reads its roles from `realm_access.roles` instead of the groups claim sets `realm_roles: true` in its `meta/rbac.yml`. [10_realm_role_grants.yml](../../../../roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/update/10_realm_role_grants.yml) then creates one realm role `<application_id>-<role>` per declared role, `administrator` included, and grants it to the matching group. Every realm user also holds `default-roles-<realm>`, which the application can map to its lowest role so that nobody without a role group is locked out."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application whose gate requires no role group keeps the default oauth2-proxy pages."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application whose gate requires role groups (``services.sso.oauth2.allowed_groups``) answers with its own oauth2-proxy 403 page, `error.html.j2 <templates/sso_proxy/error.html.j2>`__. `sso_proxy.yml <../web-app-keycloak/tasks/sso_proxy.yml>`__ renders it next to the gate’s configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application whose gate requires role groups (`services.sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`) answers with its own oauth2-proxy 403 page, [error.html.j2](templates/sso_proxy/error.html.j2). [sso_proxy.yml](../web-app-keycloak/tasks/sso_proxy.yml) renders it next to the gate's configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "An application whose own sign-in page offers more than one way to sign in declares every method it offers under its entity in `meta/services.yml`, so that each method can be switched on its own and the page shows only what the deployment mode allows."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application whose registration rejects the shell-safe alphabet states that in its own meta/users.yml rather than carrying a second credential beside the account it already owns."
msgstr "Une demande dont l'enregistrement rejette l'alphabet shell-safe indique que dans sa propre meta/users.yml plutôt que de porter un deuxième titre à côté du compte qu'il possède déjà."

msgid "An application with a domain and TLS of its own gets the CA when its resolved TLS mode is self-signed. Otherwise it gets it only when one of its services declares ``ca_client: true`` and the SSO issuer application it calls resolves TLS enabled and self-signed."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An application's canonical primary domain when it has at most max_length characters, otherwise its short entity name (e.g. ``keycloak``)."
msgstr "Domaine primaire canonique d'une application quand elle a au plus max_length caractères, sinon son nom d'entité courte (Par exemple ``keycloak``)."

msgid "An autonomous routine meets an `ask` rule only at a declared gate node; an `ask` hit anywhere else is reported as a firewall misconfiguration."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An axis the token leaves open matches anything, so ``web-app-x`` covers every row of that role and ``web-app-x#2@swarm`` only its swarm deploy of variant 2. Reads the strings a matrix entry carries, not a discovery row's native types."
msgstr "Un axe que le jeton laisse ouvert correspond à tout, donc ``web-app-x`` couvre chaque rangée de ce rôle et ``web-app-x#2@swarm`` seulement son essaim déploiement de la variante 2. Lit les chaînes qu'une entrée de matrice porte, pas les types natifs d'une ligne de découverte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An embedding model, a deprecated model and a model that denies system messages are never routed to"
msgstr "Un modèle d'intégration, un modèle déprécié et un modèle qui nie les messages système ne sont jamais acheminés vers"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` sends no header at all."
msgstr "Un vide `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` n'envoie aucun en-tête."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`` sends no header at all."
msgstr "Un vide ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`` n'envoie aucun en-tête."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty body is rejected."
msgstr "Un corps vide est rejeté."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty mapping or list returns the empty string so the surrounding template stays valid YAML (no orphan ``depends_on:`` keyword)."
msgstr "Une carte ou une liste vide retourne la chaîne vide de sorte que le modèle environnant reste valide YAML (Pas d'orphelin ``depends_on:`` Mots clés)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty or unresolvable closure filters nothing: discovery that silently dropped every provider would look exactly like a deployment without any, which is the failure this module refuses to produce elsewhere."
msgstr "Une fermeture vide ou insolvable ne filtre rien : découverte que chaque fournisseur a laissé tomber en silence ressemblerait exactement à un déploiement sans aucun, ce qui est l'échec que ce module refuse de produire ailleurs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty result is cached under its id too, or a role without the file would re-stat it on every call."
msgstr "Un résultat vide est également mis en cache sous son id, ou un rôle sans le fichier le re-staterait sur chaque appel."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty string is a valid answer: a provider that has not minted its credential yet is the normal state early in a play, and the callers distinguish it from a wrong one by probing."
msgstr "Une chaîne vide est une réponse valide : un fournisseur qui n'a pas encore son justificatif est l'état normal au début d'une pièce de théâtre, et les appelants la distinguent d'une mauvaise par une recherche."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An empty string means \"not configured\" and passes every check, which is what makes an optional provider key expressible: declare the shape, leave the value empty, and the consumer gates on emptiness."
msgstr "Une chaîne vide signifie \"non configuré\" et passe chaque contrôle, ce qui rend une clé de fournisseur optionnelle expressible: déclarer la forme, laisser la valeur vide, et les portes du consommateur sur le vide."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An enabled adapter declares everything it is allowed to do"
msgstr "Un adaptateur activé déclare tout ce qu'il est autorisé à faire"

msgid "An entry fires when its schedule matches and its condition (if any) holds. While the gate lock is held, a ``start`` entry does not fire; a ``pause`` entry still does, so the gate can quiesce a lane. A ``start`` whose routine the owner has put on hold, or that carries a recorded owner-only blocker, does not fire either: a cron re-delivery is never read as fresh consent, so the routine stays quiet across every later firing until the owner lifts the hold or clears the blocker."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry in `whitelist` or `priority` is a role name that MAY pin the axes the row would otherwise be assigned. Two spellings are accepted:"
msgstr "Une entrée dans `whitelist` ou `priority` est un nom de rôle qui PEUT épingler les axes de la ligne serait autrement assigné. Deux orthographes sont acceptées :"

msgid "An entry that fails the judgement is retranslated with the engine that produced it excluded (the gateway's `exclude` list on `/translate`). Every entry counts its attempts; after `agents.translator.max_attempts` failed attempts (default 3) it stays marked for a human and appears in the translator's report as a string no local engine can render. No entry is retried without a changed engine."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry the server already answered with a damaged span is skipped. The answer is deterministic for an unchanged source, so asking again spends a masking pass, a request and an inference to arrive at the same refusal. The mark rides in the entry's comments, so gettext drops it the moment the source changes and the entry is offered again by itself."
msgstr "Une entrée que le serveur a déjà répondu avec une portée endommagée est ignorée. La réponse est déterministe pour une source inchangée, donc demander à nouveau dépense un laissez-passer masque, une demande et une inférence pour arriver au même refus. La marque circule dans les commentaires de l'entrée, donc gettext la dépose au moment où la source change et l'entrée est offerte à nouveau par elle-même."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry therefore carries `enforce_filesystem`, true when a human left the row no choice: a `/filesystem` selection token, or a run whose `filesystem` input names exactly one kind."
msgstr "Une entrée porte donc `enforce_filesystem`, c'est vrai qu'un humain n'a pas le choix : `/filesystem` jeton de sélection, ou une course dont `filesystem` les noms d'entrée exactement un genre."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry whose ``version:`` is not a semver (a branch name, say) states an intent this cannot second-guess and is skipped."
msgstr "Une entrée dont ``version:`` n'est pas un semver (un nom de branche,) indique une intention qui ne peut pas se contredire et est ignorée."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry with overrides produces a derived shape (for example WordPress Multisite domains)."
msgstr "Une entrée avec des rebords produit une forme dérivée (par exemple les domaines WordPress Multisite)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An entry without a pinned version can never be confirmed from disk and is always reported, so the caller falls through to a real install."
msgstr "Une entrée sans version épinglée ne peut jamais être confirmée à partir du disque et est toujours signalée, de sorte que l'appelant tombe à travers une installation réelle."

msgid "An environment override points every make target at another stack."
msgstr ""

msgid "An error in the agent's own posted text is corrected at once and named."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "An example of how to use this role in your playbook:"
