# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The journey itself is not dropped. [`files/playwright/test-native-login.js`](./files/playwright/test-native-login.js) drives both personas through Funkwhale's own chain: `/login`, the Keycloak round trip whenever the proxy gates that route, then Funkwhale's own sign-in form, an authenticated-surface assertion, and sign-out back to the anonymous state. It is skipped when `services.ldap.enabled` is false, because no persona holds a Funkwhale account in that variant. The `guest` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "Le voyage lui-même n'est pas abandonné. [`files/playwright/test-native-login.js`](./files/playwright/test-native-login.js) conduit les deux personas à travers Funkwhale's propre chaîne: `/login`, les Keycloak aller-retour chaque fois que les portes proxy que l'itinéraire, alors Funkwhale'son propre signe-in, une affirmation de surface authentifiée, et de retour à l'état anonyme. Il est sauté quand `services.ldap.enabled` est faux, parce qu'aucune personne n'a Funkwhale compte dans cette variante. Les `guest` persona et les affirmations de base fonctionnent sans condition."

msgid "The journey itself is not dropped. ```files/playwright/test-admin-native.js`` <./files/playwright/test-admin-native.js>`__ drives it through Shopware’s own selectors: an authenticated backend assertion, then logout through the user-actions toggle and back to the login page. ``SSO_SERVICE_ENABLED`` selects how it signs in — through the ``a.heptacom-admin-open-auth--button`` provider link that AdminOpenAuth appends into ``.sw-login__content`` when SSO is on, through the native password form when it is off. The ``guest`` persona and the role-local reachability, TLS and HSTS assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr ""

