# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These primitives are entity-keyed. The app-keyed orchestrator [apps.sh](../apps.sh) maps app ids to entities and drives them in sequence alongside the token-store wipe in [tokens.py](../../../../utils/cleanup/tokens.py)."
msgstr "Ces primitifs sont marqués par l'entité. L'orchestreur à clé app [apps.sh](../apps.sh) maps app ids aux entités et les conduit en séquence à côté du jeton-store essuie dans [tokens.py](../../../../utils/cleanup/tokens.py)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These principles govern how teams collaborate, plan, and deliver work. For code design principles, see [principles.md](../design/principles.md)."
msgstr "Ces principes régissent la façon dont les équipes collaborent, planifient et exécutent le travail. Pour les principes de conception de code, voir [principles.md](../design/principles.md)."

msgid "These roles declare an `extensions:` key that is **not** an application addon but a database/cache engine feature, provisioned at the storage layer. These MUST stay where they are and MUST NOT move into `meta/addons/`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "These roles install nothing of their own, so the question this page answers does not arise for them: ``drv-non-free``, ``svc-ai-robot``, ``svc-swarm-manager``, ``svc-swarm-node``, ``update``, ``web-app-email``, ``web-app-navigator``."
msgstr ""

msgid "These roles log a user in from an identity header that openresty sets after oauth2-proxy verified the session. Openresty is the trust boundary: every proxying location blanks the headers listed in `TRUSTED_IDENTITY_HEADERS` of [header_trust.py](../../../../utils/roles/header_trust.py) before it sets its own, so a client cannot forge them. A published backend port bypasses that boundary, which is why these backends bind `DOCKER_BIND_HOST` and publish no `ports.local` port in swarm. A proxy secret, where present, is a second gate: the backend accepts the header only together with a secret that only openresty sends."
msgstr ""

msgid "These roles remain out of shared MCP discovery. A future exception requires a new requirement with a fixed operation list, dedicated identity, isolation boundary, human approval for mutations, and audit trail."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These roles stay out of shared MCP discovery. A future exception requires a new record with a fixed operation list, dedicated identity, isolation boundary, human approval for mutations, and audit trail."
msgstr "Ces rôles restent à l'écart de la découverte partagée du MCP. Une exception future exige un nouveau dossier avec une liste d'opérations fixes, une identité spécifique, une limite d'isolement, une approbation humaine pour les mutations et une piste de vérification."

msgid "These roles were no migration target and gained their addons later through the [integration matrix](027-integration-matrix.md) wiring; the same test keeps their rows current."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These rules are enforced via branch protection. See [branch.md](artefact/git/branch.md) for the full policy."
msgstr "Ces règles sont appliquées par le biais de la protection des succursales. Voir [branch.md](artefact/git/branch.md) pour la politique complète."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These rules keep shared role values explicit, reusable, and easy to read."
msgstr "Ces règles maintiennent des valeurs de rôle partagées explicites, réutilisables et faciles à lire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These scripts are the SPOT for repository identity resolution."
msgstr "Ces scripts sont le SPOT pour la résolution de l'identité du dépôt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These scripts keep PR scope detection, branch-prefix validation, and fork merge-ref resolution together in one place. The `🧩 Subset` label's PR-body parser lives in the `cli.meta.ci.subset_roles` module; the dispatcher [pr_affected_roles.sh](../../../github/resolve/pr_affected_roles.sh) selects between it and the diff resolver. See the \"Subset label\" section in [pipeline.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md)."
msgstr "Ces scripts maintiennent ensemble la détection de portée PR, la validation de préfixe de branche et la résolution de fusion-ref de fourche en un seul endroit. Les `🧩 Subset` l'analyseur PR-body de l'étiquette vit dans le `cli.meta.ci.subset_roles` module; le régulateur [pr_affected_roles.sh](../../../github/resolve/pr_affected_roles.sh) sélectionne entre elle et le résolveur de diff. Voir \"Étiquette de sous-ensemble\" rubrique [pipeline.md](../../../../docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These scripts run **on the deployed host**, not on the controller. `test-e2e-cli` renders `templates/test.env.j2` into the environment and calls `test.sh`, which orchestrates the rest. They use `systemctl`, the `container` wrapper and `/etc/machine-id`, so they only make sense where the role actually deployed."
msgstr "Ces scripts sont exécutés **sur l'hôte déployé**Pas sur le contrôleur. `test-e2e-cli` rendus `templates/test.env.j2` dans l'environnement et les appels `test.sh`, qui orchestre le reste. Ils utilisent `systemctl`, les `container` emballage et `/etc/machine-id`, donc ils n'ont de sens que là où le rôle effectivement déployé."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These scripts run inside the local infinito container and remove container-local state only. For the canonical Make target index that invokes these helpers, see [make.md](../../../docs/contributing/tools/make.md)."
msgstr "Ces scripts s'exécutent à l'intérieur du conteneur Infinito local et suppriment l'état conteneur-local seulement. Pour l'index canonique Make cible qui invoque ces aides, voir [make.md](../../../docs/contributing/tools/make.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These steps are the shared repository workflow and apply regardless of whether you work on Linux, macOS, or Windows with WSL2."
msgstr "Ces étapes sont le flux de travail du dépôt partagé et s'appliquent que vous travailliez sur Linux, macOS ou Windows avec WSL2."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These templates are intended for inclusion in larger NGINX configuration files via Jinja2.   They modularize your configuration by separating HTML, WebSocket, and media proxying, allowing for clear, reusable, and maintainable reverse proxy logic."
msgstr "Ces modèles sont destinés à être inclus dans des fichiers de configuration NGINX plus grands via Jinja2. Ils modulent votre configuration en séparant HTML, WebSocket et proxy media, permettant une logique de proxy inverse claire, réutilisable et durable."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "These variables cap the `infinito` container so local runs can reproduce GitHub-hosted runner pressure. Each default is `0`, which Docker interprets as \"unlimited\" and is identical to omitting the key. See [ci.md](../../actions/debugging/ci.md) for runner specs and reproduction profiles."
msgstr "Ces variables plafonnent `infinito` conteneur afin que les parcours locaux puissent reproduire la pression de coureur de GitHub. Chaque défaut est `0`, que Docker interprète comme \"unlimited\" et est identique à l'omission de la clé. Voir [ci.md](../../actions/debugging/ci.md) pour les spécifications de coureur et les profils de reproduction."

msgid "These web templates are generated from the one template for the `human` audience. You MUST NOT edit them by hand; regenerate them with `python -m cli.contributing.pull_request default`. The lint [test_pull_request_template_current.py](../../../../tests/lint/repository/test_pull_request_template_current.py) fails when one is not the current render."
msgstr ""

msgid "They are also the rows a run must not sample. A priority row is deployed in **every combination it can take** — each variant, in each mode its role offers, and on the modes that carry the network axis once per node network mode the role can be served in (`clearnet`, `tor`, `multi`) — all within the same sweep. A 3-variant role offering compose and swarm therefore becomes 3 × 2 × 3 = **18 jobs**, not 3. That is the point of naming a role in `priority`: it is proven everywhere at once instead of over several sweeps."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "They live apart from the client itself because the generator runs on the bare bootstrap interpreter: importing the client would pull in the language table and with it a YAML parser the generator is not allowed to need."
msgstr "Ils vivent en dehors du client lui-même parce que le générateur fonctionne sur l'interprète de bootstrap nu: importer le client tirerait dans la table de langue et avec elle un analyseur YAML le générateur n'est pas autorisé à avoir besoin."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "They live at ``meta/services.yml.<primary_entity>.{run_after,lifecycle}`` where ``<primary_entity>`` is the value returned by :func:`utils.roles.entity.name.entity_name` for the role's directory name."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "They live at ``secrets.credentials``, which is where the roles' own vars and every other consumer address them. Reading the top-level ``credentials`` instead returns nothing for every provider whose ``credential.source`` is ``credentials``, and the deploy then aborts on a secret that was provisioned all along."
msgstr "Ils vivent à ``secrets.credentials``, où les rôles propres et tous les autres consommateurs s'adressent à eux. Lire le haut niveau ``credentials`` ne renvoie rien pour chaque fournisseur dont ``credential.source`` est ``credentials``, et le déploiement avorte alors sur un secret qui a été fourni tout le long."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "They must not contain application-specific configuration values."
msgstr "Ils ne doivent pas contenir de valeurs de configuration spécifiques à l'application."

msgid "They protect service-to-service traffic and are independent of the user boundary."
msgstr ""

