msgid "This role deploys no third-party application, so the licence above is the only one that applies."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys nothing. Its ``meta/services.yml`` pins the image and release each distribution’s development environment boots from, keyed by the distribution id of `meta/distros.yml <../../meta/distros.yml>`__, and ``utils/distros.py`` reads the workspace matrix from it. Because the pins live in a role’s ``meta/services.yml``, the docker updater proposes new releases as pull requests and the image mirror and the vulnerability scan cover them like every other role image. ``follow: latest`` holds a pin to the release the ``latest`` tag points at, so Ubuntu moves between LTS releases only and Fedora skips rawhide. Arch stays rolling, and CentOS Stream tags carry no number the updater can order, so its next stream is a manual change."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys nothing. Its `meta/services.yml` pins the image and release each distribution's development environment boots from, keyed by the distribution id of [meta/distros.yml](../../meta/distros.yml), and `utils/distros.py` reads the workspace matrix from it. Because the pins live in a role's `meta/services.yml`, the docker updater proposes new releases as pull requests and the image mirror and the vulnerability scan cover them like every other role image. `follow: latest` holds a pin to the release the `latest` tag points at, so Ubuntu moves between LTS releases only and Fedora skips rawhide. Arch stays rolling, and CentOS Stream tags carry no number the updater can order, so its next stream is a manual change."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the LiteLLM admin UI as the browser-facing entry point of the headless LiteLLM Gateway. It runs in host mode and starts no container of its own: it claims a canonical domain, terminates TLS, applies the platform Content-Security-Policy, and reverse-proxies that domain to the local HTTP port the gateway publishes. Visitors sign in with the gateway's own UI credentials."
msgstr "Ce rôle déploie l'interface utilisateur d'administration LiteLLM comme point d'entrée du navigateur sans tête LiteLLM Gateway. Il fonctionne en mode hôte et ne démarre aucun conteneur à lui seul : il revendique un domaine canonique, met fin à TLS, applique la plate-forme Content-Security-Policy et inverse-proxies que le domaine au port HTTP local que publie la passerelle. Les visiteurs s'inscrivent avec les propres identifiants d'interface utilisateur de la passerelle."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the LiteLLM admin UI as the browser-facing entry point of the headless LiteLLM Gateway. It runs in host mode and starts no container of its own: it claims a canonical domain, terminates TLS, applies the platform Content-Security-Policy, and reverse-proxies that domain to the local HTTP port the gateway publishes. Visitors sign in with the gateway’s own UI credentials."
msgstr "Ce rôle déploie l'interface utilisateur d'administration LiteLLM comme point d'entrée du navigateur sans tête LiteLLM Gateway. Il fonctionne en mode hôte et ne démarre aucun conteneur à lui seul : il revendique un domaine canonique, met fin à TLS, applique la plate-forme Content-Security-Policy et inverse-proxies que le domaine au port HTTP local que publie la passerelle. Les visiteurs se connectent avec les propres identifiants d'interface utilisateur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the OpenTalk stack using Docker Compose and exposes the web frontend at ``open.talk.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}`` through the central reverse proxy. It runs the Rust controller, the LiveKit WebRTC media server, the React web frontend, a dedicated Redis, a dedicated MinIO bucket for controller assets, a RabbitMQ broker, and the OpenTalk recorder for meeting MP4 archives. The deployment integrates with the shared Keycloak realm via OIDC and reuses ``svc-db-postgres`` and ``web-svc-coturn`` for relational data and STUN/TURN. For identity wiring details see `IAM.md <docs/IAM.md>`__ and `LDAP.md <docs/LDAP.md>`__."
msgstr "Ce rôle OpenTalk pile en utilisant Docker Compose et expose le web frontend à ``open.talk.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}`` par le proxy central inverse. Il exécute le contrôleur Rust, le serveur multimédia WebRTC LiveKit, le frontend web React, un Redis, une MinIO pour les actifs du contrôleur, RabbitMQ le courtier, OpenTalk enregistreur pour la réunion MP4 les archives. Le déploiement s'intègre à la Keycloak OIDC et réutilisations ``svc-db-postgres`` et ``web-svc-coturn`` pour les données relationnelles et STUN/TURN. Pour les détails de câblage d'identité voir `IAM.md <docs/IAM.md>`__ et `LDAP.md <docs/LDAP.md>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the OpenTalk stack using Docker Compose and exposes the web frontend at `open.talk.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}` through the central reverse proxy. It runs the Rust controller, the LiveKit WebRTC media server, the React web frontend, a dedicated Redis, a dedicated MinIO bucket for controller assets, a RabbitMQ broker, and the OpenTalk recorder for meeting MP4 archives. The deployment integrates with the shared Keycloak realm via OIDC and reuses `svc-db-postgres` and `web-svc-coturn` for relational data and STUN/TURN. For identity wiring details see [IAM.md](docs/IAM.md) and [LDAP.md](docs/LDAP.md)."
msgstr "Ce rôle OpenTalk pile en utilisant Docker Compose et expose le web frontend à `open.talk.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}` par le proxy central inverse. Il exécute le contrôleur Rust, le serveur multimédia WebRTC LiveKit, le frontend web React, un Redis, une MinIO pour les actifs du contrôleur, RabbitMQ le courtier, OpenTalk enregistreur pour la réunion MP4 les archives. Le déploiement s'intègre à la Keycloak OIDC et réutilisations `svc-db-postgres` et `web-svc-coturn` pour les données relationnelles et STUN/TURN. Pour les détails de câblage d'identité voir [IAM.md](docs/IAM.md) et [LDAP.md](docs/LDAP.md)."

msgid "This role deploys the Python pull script that talks to each remote provider, installs the systemd service that drives it on the configured schedule (`SYS_SCHEDULE_BACKUP_REMOTE_TO_LOCAL`), and first waits for the rest of the manipulation group via `sys-lock`, up to `SYS_TIMEOUT_BACKUP_SERVICES`. The remote side must expose a chrooted SSH/SFTP endpoint that publishes its backup tree: deploy [user-backup](../user-backup/) for the chrooted pull account and [sys-ctl-cln-bkps](../sys-ctl-cln-bkps/) to keep the published tree bounded."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the Python pull script that talks to each remote provider, installs the systemd service that drives it on the configured schedule (``SYS_SCHEDULE_BACKUP_REMOTE_TO_LOCAL``), and first waits for the rest of the manipulation group via ``sys-lock``, up to ``SYS_TIMEOUT_BACKUP_SERVICES``. The remote side must expose a chrooted SSH/SFTP endpoint that publishes its backup tree: deploy `user-backup <../user-backup/>`__ for the chrooted pull account and `sys-ctl-cln-bkps <../sys-ctl-cln-bkps/>`__ to keep the published tree bounded."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the [Meta Infinite Graph](https://github.com/infinito-nexus/meta), a browsable graph of every Infinito.Nexus role and the dependencies between them. It is served as a pre-rendered static site from a project-owned container image."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the `Meta Infinite Graph <https://github.com/infinito-nexus/meta>`__, a browsable graph of every Infinito.Nexus role and the dependencies between them. It is served as a pre-rendered static site from a project-owned container image."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the broker together with a container-API socket proxy in Compose and Swarm deployments. Open WebUI reaches the broker as a second OpenAI connection and forwards the caller's identity. The broker checks the caller's Keycloak group, creates or starts that caller's agent under the isolating runtime, forwards the request to it and streams the answer back. Agents reach their model only through the broker, which relays each call to the shared LiteLLM gateway with its own key and tags it with the owner."
msgstr "Ce rôle déploie le courtier avec un conteneurAPI proxy socket dans les déploiements de Compose et Swarm. Open WebUI rejoint le courtier comme une deuxième connexion OpenAI et transmet l'identité de l'appelant. Le courtier vérifie l'appelant Keycloak groupe, crée ou démarre l'agent de l'appelant sous le runtime d'isolement, lui transmet la demande et retourne la réponse. Les agents n'atteignent leur modèle que par l'intermédiaire du courtier, qui relaie chaque appel à la passerelle LiteLLM partagée avec sa propre clé et la tagge avec le propriétaire."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role deploys the broker together with a container-API socket proxy in Compose and Swarm deployments. Open WebUI reaches the broker as a second OpenAI connection and forwards the caller’s identity. The broker checks the caller’s Keycloak group, creates or starts that caller’s agent under the isolating runtime, forwards the request to it and streams the answer back. Agents reach their model only through the broker, which relays each call to the shared LiteLLM gateway with its own key and tags it with the owner."
msgstr "Ce rôle déploie le courtier avec un conteneurAPI proxy socket dans les déploiements de Compose et Swarm. Open WebUI atteint le courtier comme une deuxième connexion OpenAI et transmet l'identité de l'appelant. Le courtier vérifie les appelants Keycloak groupe, crée ou démarre cet agent de l'appelant dans le cadre de l'exécution d'isolement, lui transmet la demande et retourne la réponse. Les agents n'atteignent leur modèle que par l'intermédiaire du courtier, qui relaie chaque appel à la passerelle LiteLLM partagée avec sa propre clé et la tagge avec le propriétaire."

msgid "This role deploys the fixture with Docker Compose behind the standard front proxy, building a small custom nginx image from the tree under ``files/app``. The role refuses to run unless the inventory sets ``AGENT_FIXTURE_BUNDLE: true``; only the agents test bundle (``inventories/bundles/servers/agents``) sets that flag, so the fixture never comes up on a real host and any other inventory fails hard at the first task."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the fixture with Docker Compose behind the standard front proxy, building a small custom nginx image from the tree under `files/app`. The role refuses to run unless the inventory sets `AGENT_FIXTURE_BUNDLE: true`; only the agents test bundle (`inventories/bundles/servers/agents`) sets that flag, so the fixture never comes up on a real host and any other inventory fails hard at the first task."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "This role deploys the official ``jitsi/{web,prosody,jicofo,jvb}`` images as a single-domain Jitsi Meet stack. With SSO enabled, the oauth2-proxy gate admits every realm user to the vhost. With ``services.keycloak_adapter.enabled`` also true, the role builds the `nordeck jitsi-keycloak-adapter <https://github.com/nordeck/jitsi-keycloak-adapter>`__ (Apache-2.0) and switches prosody to ``AUTH_TYPE=jwt``. In the LDAP-only variant, prosody uses the image’s own ``AUTH_TYPE=ldap`` path (``mod_auth_cyrus`` against the saslauthd the ``LDAP_*`` variables of `env.j2 <./templates/env.j2>`__ configure). The web container sits behind the central openresty reverse proxy at ``meet.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}``; the media plane (jvb) publishes UDP ``10000/udp`` on the host."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "This role deploys the official `jitsi/{web,prosody,jicofo,jvb}` images as a single-domain Jitsi Meet stack. With SSO enabled, the oauth2-proxy gate admits every realm user to the vhost. With `services.keycloak_adapter.enabled` also true, the role builds the [nordeck jitsi-keycloak-adapter](https://github.com/nordeck/jitsi-keycloak-adapter) (Apache-2.0) and switches prosody to `AUTH_TYPE=jwt`. In the LDAP-only variant, prosody uses the image's own `AUTH_TYPE=ldap` path (`mod_auth_cyrus` against the saslauthd the `LDAP_*` variables of [env.j2](./templates/env.j2) configure). The web container sits behind the central openresty reverse proxy at `meet.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}`; the media plane (jvb) publishes UDP `10000/udp` on the host."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the single-node Wazuh stack (``wazuh.manager``, ``wazuh.indexer``, ``wazuh.dashboard``) with Docker Compose or Docker Swarm. A one-shot ``wazuh-certs-generator`` job creates the internal TLS material before the manager and the indexer start. The indexer is the stack’s own datastore and holds the OpenSearch security configuration, so the role needs no shared database. Agent enrollment is not part of this role: the agent ports are declared in `services.yml <./meta/services.yml>`__ but not published. The manager’s vulnerability detection data (``/var/ossec/queue/vd``, volume ``wazuh_manager_vd``) is deliberately not backed up. The manager downloads it again after a restore, which can take a long time. This matters once agents are enrolled."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the single-node Wazuh stack (`wazuh.manager`, `wazuh.indexer`, `wazuh.dashboard`) with Docker Compose or Docker Swarm. A one-shot `wazuh-certs-generator` job creates the internal TLS material before the manager and the indexer start. The indexer is the stack's own datastore and holds the OpenSearch security configuration, so the role needs no shared database. Agent enrollment is not part of this role: the agent ports are declared in [services.yml](./meta/services.yml) but not published. The manager's vulnerability detection data (`/var/ossec/queue/vd`, volume `wazuh_manager_vd`) is deliberately not backed up. The manager downloads it again after a restore, which can take a long time. This matters once agents are enrolled."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the upstream render server image, which serves the editor at `/` and the render queue at `/renders/`. The server puts everything except its login page behind its own login form. When Keycloak is part of the deployment, the oauth2 gate additionally guards the whole domain, so only signed-in platform users reach that form."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role deploys the upstream render server image, which serves the editor at ``/`` and the render queue at ``/renders/``. The server puts everything except its login page behind its own login form. When Keycloak is part of the deployment, the oauth2 gate additionally guards the whole domain, so only signed-in platform users reach that form."
