# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role gives every other role one place to put packet filter rules. A role that needs them writes ``templates/nftables.conf.j2`` declaring its own nftables table and includes this role; the fragment is rendered to ``/etc/nftables.d/<role>.conf``, checked, loaded, and read back, so a deploy fails rather than quietly leaving a gap. Deployed on its own, the role installs nftables, the ruleset that loads every fragment, and the ``nftables.service`` that replays them at boot."
msgstr "Ce rôle donne à chaque autre rôle un endroit pour mettre des règles de filtre de paquets. Un rôle qui en a besoin écrit ``templates/nftables.conf.j2`` la déclaration de ses propres nftables table et inclut ce rôle; le fragment est rendu à ``/etc/nftables.d/<role>.conf``, vérifié, chargé, et lu en arrière, donc un déploiement échoue plutôt que de laisser tranquillement un vide. Déployé seul, le rôle installe nftables, le jeu de règles qui charge chaque fragment, et le ``nftables.service`` qui les rejoue au démarrage."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role gives every other role one place to put packet filter rules. A role that needs them writes `templates/nftables.conf.j2` declaring its own nftables table and includes this role; the fragment is rendered to `/etc/nftables.d/<role>.conf`, checked, loaded, and read back, so a deploy fails rather than quietly leaving a gap. Deployed on its own, the role installs nftables, the ruleset that loads every fragment, and the `nftables.service` that replays them at boot."
