msgid "`FLOWISE_USERNAME` and `FLOWISE_PASSWORD` in `templates/env.j2` are read by no Flowise 3.1.4 code path (absent from `server-commands-base.ts` and `.env.example`; measured in the container: no file under `node_modules/flowise/dist` or `flowise-components/dist` names either key, while `FLOWISE_SECRETKEY_OVERWRITE` appears 8 times), so they create no account and only put the administrator password into the container environment; the instance account is `flowise-api-bot`, registered by `tasks/utils/owner.yml`. Option: drop both keys."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` turns the cancel into an escalation. A cancel request does not stop a running step: the runner asks it to end, and a step that ignores the signal keeps going until its own `timeout-minutes`, which is 350 for a deploy. The concurrency group holds the newer run on `pending` until the occupant is *terminal*, not until it is cancel-requested, so a superseded sweep can block its branch for hours after being told to stop -- measured at eight minutes and counting, with ten deploy jobs untouched. After the wait, every run that is still not `completed` gets [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), which bypasses the conditions that keep it alive. The skipped cleanup steps are the price, and for a run that has already been superseded its artefacts are of no use to anyone. Leave the variable unset to cancel and walk away, which is what a closed pull request and a deleted branch want."
msgstr "`FORCE_CANCEL_AFTER_SECONDS` transforme l'annulation en escalade. Une demande d'annulation n'arrête pas une étape de course : le coureur lui demande de se terminer, et une étape qui ignore le signal continue jusqu'à ce que sa propre `timeout-minutes`, qui est 350 pour un déploiement. Le groupe concurrency tient le nouveau `pending` jusqu'à ce que l'occupant soit *terminal*, pas jusqu'à ce qu'il soit annulé-requête , de sorte qu'un balayage remplacé peut bloquer sa branche pendant des heures après avoir été dit d'arrêter -- mesurée à huit minutes et comptant , avec dix déploiements intouchés . Après l'attente, chaque course qui n'est toujours pas `completed` obtient [`force-cancel`](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs), qui contourne les conditions qui le maintiennent en vie. Les étapes de nettoyage escamotées sont le prix, et pour une course qui a déjà été remplacée ses artefacts ne sont d'aucune utilité pour personne. Laisser la variable déconnecter pour annuler et partir, ce qui est ce que veut une requête de tirage fermé et une branche supprimée."

msgid "`FUSIONDIRECTORY_ADMIN_USER` and `FUSIONDIRECTORY_ADMIN_PASS` in `templates/env.j2` have no effect: they are variables of the separate `nfrastack/openldap-fusiondirectory` image, and the `nfrastack/fusiondirectory:1.5` application image reads neither (absent from its `defaults-40-fusiondirectory`, `functions-40-fusiondirectory` and `init-40-fusiondirectory`). The administrator signs in as the platform persona that `svc-db-openldap` provisions, granted by `files/shell/ldap/bootstrap.sh`. Options: drop both keys."
