# ``[entity_name]`` pour shared_net, ``[]`` pour default_net
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: liste des alias DNS. Par défaut & #160;: ``[entity_name]`` pour shared_net, ``[]`` pour default_net"

msgid "``all`` needs a dnsmasq built with ``nftset`` (2.87 or newer) for direct host names; CentOS Stream 10 ships one without it, so there the deploy refuses direct host names and accepts addresses and CIDRs only. ``all`` is also refused in swarm mode, on a dnsmasq other drop-ins share or whose ``/etc/dnsmasq.conf`` names its own upstreams, on a dnsmasq that resolves as root or nobody or shares its UID, when the Tor group already exists on the host, and when ``networks.internet.dns`` lies inside the resolver set."
msgstr ""

msgid "``all`` sends every outbound connection of the node and its containers through Tor and fails closed: TCP goes to the TransPort, every other protocol to an unlisted destination is dropped, and names outside the direct list resolve only through Tor’s DNSPort. DNS reaches only loopback, the bridge and the deployed roles’ own subnets, so no LAN resolver answers beside Tor; systemd-resolved, resolv.conf and the docker daemon lose their clearnet fallback. When Tor is down, that traffic fails; there is no clearnet fallback. Compose only."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (par défaut ``True``): le fichier (ou d'une entrée par voie pointillée) Peut-être être présent pour un rôle de ce type. Jeu ``allowed: False`` interdire le fichier/entrée sur les rôles de ce type afin que la couche de linte puisse faire surface l'infraction avec une raison précise."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` seulement porte ``docker0`` une fois le démon a couru, et la config de démon est écrite avant que sur un noeud frais - les faits sont rassemblés au début du jeu, et rien ne les rassemble après l'installation. La lecture du fait seul ne donne donc rien sur la même piste qui doit émettre l'adresse, ce qui laisse les conteneurs intérieurs pointés sur le résolveur de clearnet et le contrôle DinD DNS en échec sur un domaine que le noeud dnsmasq connaît."

